	(gr_text_box "1. FABRICATE PCB IN ACCORDANCE WITH IPC-6012F CLASS 2.\n\n2. FINISHED PCB ACCEPTABILITY PER IPC-A-600M CLASS 2.\n\n3. BASE MATERIAL: FR-4, Tg > 170°C, CAF RESISTANT, UL 94 V-0.\n\n4. LAMINATE MATERIAL SHALL COMPLY WITH IPC-4101F.\n\n5. LAYER COUNT, STACK-UP, BOARD THICKNESS AND COPPER WEIGHTS AS SPECIFIED IN THE STACK-UP DRAWING.\n\n6. COPPER WEIGHTS IN THE STACK-UP REPRESENT STARTING FOIL WEIGHTS. FINISHED CONDUCTOR AND PLATED-HOLE COPPER THICKNESSES SHALL COMPLY WITH IPC-6012F CLASS 2.\n\n7. SOLDER MASK: LPI, BOTH SIDES, COMPLIANT WITH IPC-SM-840E, CLASS H.\n\n8. VIA TENTING SHALL FOLLOW THE SOLDER MASK GERBER DATA. VIA FILLING OR PLUGGING IS NOT REQUIRED UNLESS OTHERWISE SPECIFIED.\n\n9. SURFACE FINISH: LEAD-FREE HASL, PER IPC-6012F.\n\n10. PCB MATERIALS AND FINISHES SHALL COMPLY WITH EU RoHS DIRECTIVE 2011/65/EU, AS AMENDED.\n\n11. 100% ELECTRICAL CONTINUITY AND ISOLATION TEST REQUIRED.\n\n12. MATERIAL OR PROCESS SUBSTITUTIONS REQUIRE APPROVAL.\n\n13. THE SUPPLIED GERBER AND NC DRILL FILES SHALL BE THE AUTHORITATIVE SOURCE FOR PCB GEOMETRY, BOARD OUTLINE, COPPER FEATURES AND HOLE LOCATIONS/SIZES. DIMENSIONS AND LAYER IMAGES SHOWN IN THIS DOCUMENT ARE FOR REFERENCE ONLY. IN CASE OF DISCREPANCY, THE FABRICATION DATA SHALL TAKE PRECEDENCE."
		(start 30 40)
		(end 110 131.223476)
